[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'If I was a brand new real estate agent trying to get my first 10 listings, I wouldn\'t start by posting generic home tours and just hoping buyers would find me. Personally, I would use an AI tool called HeyGen to build three different types of videos. Videos that make local homeowners aware of me, videos that'

[00:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'prove I understand the selling process, and personalized videos that give specific homeowners a reason to respond. So, in this video, I\'m going to show you the exact system that I\'m going to be building inside of HeyGen, including the prompts, videos, and how I would turn'

[00:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'those videos into actual listing conversations. Now, AI isn\'t going to magically hand you listings, but it can help you show up consistently, build trust before the first call, and follow up without filming a new video every'

[00:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'day. But now, let\'s not stall. Let\'s just get started building the system. Now, the first thing I would do is pick one specific market, not an entire state, and not every city within an hour of me. One town, one neighborhood, or one type of homeowner that I want to'

[00:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'serve. Your videos become much more convincing when they\'re made for a specific kind of person. Instead of saying, "Here\'s what\'s happening in real estate," you could say, "Here\'s what homeowners in this neighborhood should know before they sell." But now, for this walkthrough, I\'m building a system'

[01:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'for a fictional agent targeting homeowners in Oak Ridge. The goal is to become the agent that sellers recognize before they sell. But before I create anything, I need accurate source material. On the side here, I\'ve got my approved market report, my agent bio, my'

[01:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'brokerage information, brand assets, a seller guide, and testimonials that I have permission to use. Additionally, I would confirm every price, date, market statistic, contact detail, and required'

[01:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'disclosures before giving anything to AI. HeyGen can build a video for you, but the agent is still responsible for making sure the information\'s accurate. You also need to follow your brokerage rules, your local advertising requirements, MLS media permissions, and'

[01:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'fair housing laws. Do not upload private client information, and do not use property photos or listing media unless you have the right permission. But now, we can open up HeyGen, and the first thing I would do is create a brand'

[01:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'system. You add your logo, your brand font, the colors, headshots, and any other approved photos or videos you might want to add. This seriously only takes a few minutes, but it helps each one of your videos feel super consistent. A homeowner may see one'

[02:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'video on YouTube, one on Instagram, and the third one inside of an email, and they should recognize immediately that all three of them came from the same agent. But next, I would create an avatar for myself. This is going to become the consistent presenter across'

[02:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the entire system. Just record your avatar footage with clear lighting and eye-level camera, clear audio, and the same natural delivery that you\'re going to use when speaking to an actual client. And once it\'s ready, you can actually create different looks for'

[02:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'different videos. A polished look for market updates, a more conversational look for social media, and a clean professional look for personalized outreach. It\'s all still the same agent, just presented in the right setting for each message. But now, the first video I'

[02:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'would create is a local market update. This is the awareness part of our system. It gives homeowners a useful reason to discover and remember you. Inside Video Agent, just attach report that you already have, add your brand assets, and any other neighborhood'

[02:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'footage or pictures that you have permission to use. Then describe the exact video that you want. This is the prompt I\'m going to be using and of course leaving down in the description below. But again, for your own video, it might look a little bit different. And'

[03:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Video Agent\'s going to use the prompt, the report, and all of the assets to make our first draft for us. Here\'s your Oakridge market update for July 2026. Let\'s break down the latest trends so you can stay informed on what your home is worth today. Median sale prices hit'

[03:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '512K, up nearly 3% from last year. And now, once that\'s done, I\'m making sure every detail matches with the information that I gave it, such as the statistics and if all the pictures match the area I\'m trying to show. If a stock footage feels'

[03:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'misleading or misrepresents the area, just replace it with approved footage. But now, this right here becomes our main video that we\'re going to be uploading this week. And now, it\'s super easy to create an updated version when the market changes. But now, our next'

[03:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'type of video is going to be building trust. Instead of telling people I\'m a real estate expert, I\'m going to answer the questions that homeowners already have and just prove it. How do I know what my home is worth? What should I repair before listing? Should I sell'

[03:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'before buying my next home? What actually happens during a listing appointment? For these videos, I would open AI studio. Just head over to the apps tab and it\'ll be right here. And on the right side bar, I would select my avatar and just create one short video'

[04:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'for each question. On the left here is the script that I\'m going to be using for this example. And I\'m going to be using the same avatar, voice, colors, and layout for the entire series. Before you spend thousands renovating your home, speak with a local agent about'

[04:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'which improvements buyers in your market actually notice. But now one recording setup has become a repeatable education series. And I can publish a new answer pretty much every single day without having to get in front of the camera.'

[04:35] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'But useful videos alone aren\'t the entire strategy. If the goal is to win listings, every video needs to lead to a clear next step. I wouldn\'t end every single video with a vague follow for more. I\'d offer something more connected to the homeowners actual problem. A'

[04:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'personalized pricing review, a seller prep checklist, a 15-minute strategy call, or a guide explaining the local selling process. The video is what\'s earning their attention and the offer gives that attention somewhere to go.'

[05:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'And all of these only take you a few minutes to do, but the upside can be huge. But now the third video is going to be where this system becomes just a little more personal. Most homeowners just receive the same generic message from every other agent. So I would'

[05:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'create a short video specifically for the new person I\'m contacting. And don\'t pretend you know anything about the homeowners plans that they haven\'t told you. Inside AI studio, I would just create one reusable outreach template. Then duplicate it and just change the'

[05:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'approved details for each new person. Here on the left we have an example. I\'ll be leaving this down in the description, too. But you can pause if you want to read it. The video never claims I inspected the property and it doesn\'t make assumptions about the'

[05:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'homeowner. It simply introduces me, offers something useful, and gives them an easy way to respond. And I would send this after somebody requests a guide, responds to a video, attends an open house, or just gives me permission to follow up. The goal is never to blast'

[05:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'hundreds of people with the same automated message. It\'s to make a legit follow-up feel more personal. But now, most listing opportunities won\'t just come from one video. They\'ll come from consistent follow-up. So, I create a small video sequence before I even need'

[06:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'it. The first video introduces me and delivers the resource that they requested. The second explains how a price review works. The third covers what to prepare before meeting an agent. And the fourth explains what happens'

[06:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'after they decide to list. These videos answer common questions before the client even joins a call. And it helps them understand what it would feel like and look like to actually work with you. But of course, I would still respond personally when they ask you a question.'

[06:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'The videos simply help you stop repeating the same thing every single time. And if I worked in a market where the homeowners speak different languages, I\'d also translate my strongest seller video. Just open video translation and upload the finished'

[06:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'video. And then you could choose what language you want based on what your audience speaks. And just a little tip, the speed and precision options include the lip sync. Also, the translated speech actually matches up with your speaker\'s lips.'

[06:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'And another side note, a brand glossary can help big here. It can help keep names, real estate terms, and neighborhoods all consistent. But now, once everything is fully built out, this is the weekly structure that I would'

[07:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'follow. On Monday, I\'d publish one local market or neighborhood video. On Wednesday, I would publish one seller question or common mistake. On Friday, I would publish a checklist, a case study, or an explanation of the listing'

[07:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'process. And of course, throughout the week, I would send personalized messages and videos to those people who requested me a follow-up or just requested more information. And each core video can be adapted to YouTube shorts, Instagram, email, and your website. But now, here\'s'

[07:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'how I would connect the content to our goal of 10 listings. The public videos create local awareness. The seller videos answer questions and build credibility. The call to action identifies homeowners who want more information. The personalized video'

[07:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'start direct conversations and the follow-up sequence helps move those conversations into real appointments. And of course, I would track every lead, which video brought them in, what they requested, when I followed up, and whether the conversation actually became'

[07:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'an appointment. Then I would keep improving the videos that generate real appointments. And let\'s keep our expectations realistic. I wouldn\'t expect 10 videos to automatically generate you 10 listings. I\'d repeat the system until I signed the first one,'

[08:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'then the second, and then eventually the 10th. The advantage of the AI is that I can keep showing up consistently through this entire process without spending every week filming and editing from scratch. But now, if you guys want to'

[08:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'build this system for your own real estate business, HeyGen is linked down in the description below and it\'s free to try right now. And if you want to learn more practical ways to use AI in real estate, subscribe to the channel because there is a lot more coming.'
